---
import Webmentions from "../components/Webmentions.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/GardenPost.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="About Me"
    description="About Joshua and who he is as a person"
    attrib="Joshua Commanding the Sun to Stand Still upon Gibeon (1816) John Martin"
    hero="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Joshua_Commanding_the_Sun_to_Stand_Still_upon_Gibeon_%281816%29_John_Martin_-_NGA_2004.64.1.jpg/2560px-Joshua_Commanding_the_Sun_to_Stand_Still_upon_Gibeon_%281816%29_John_Martin_-_NGA_2004.64.1.jpg"
>
    <section class="about">
        <p>
            I like building things. I'd say I'm a maker at heart, and my choice
            of medium to make is typically code.
        </p>
        <p>
            I spend most of my time reading, learning or building cool stuff and
            <a href="garden/solving-problems-that-annoy-me" class="garden-link"
                >solving problems that annoy me</a
            >.
        </p>

        <p>
            <a href="garden/now">Here's what im doing right now</a> and <a
                href="garden/things-i-wanna-do"
                >what I'd like to do soon.
            </a>
        </p>

        <p>
            Which has also led to me
            <a href="garden/why-i-built-this-site" class="garden-link"
                >building this digital garden</a
            >. In short, it's because I believe not everything has to scale,
            ship or perform. Some things are allowed to exist simply because
            they are useful or comforting. But I feel they do deserve to be
            jotted down somewhere, on what they were meant to be and what they
            have become and why.
        </p>

        <p>
            <a href="garden/ditching-windows-for-linux" class="garden-link"
                >I work primarily on Linux now</a
            >
            (I use Arch btw). And wish to contribute more to systems programming one
            day.
        </p>

        <p>
            If you’ve found your way here, you’re welcome to explore. This space
            isn’t meant to impress. It’s an attempt to make something honest,
            and to invite you into the gentle disorder of my thinking.
        </p>
    </section>
</Layout>
